-- EU AI Act: what may be done to me if I do not report.
-- Articles 99 and 101, and Article 75c(4) as inserted by Regulation (EU)
-- 2026/1744. Each figure is a CEILING on the fine, not a tariff: the fine
-- actually imposed depends on Article 99(7) or Article 101(1), second
-- subparagraph, which are judgments and are not encoded.
-- Money is in euros; turnover is the provider's total worldwide annual
-- turnover for the preceding financial year, an input.
-- DRAFT. Not for use as advice. See NOTES.md.
--
-- THE CENTRAL FINDING (F8 in NOTES.md). Article 99(4) fixes ceilings for the
-- obligations of providers "pursuant to Article 16". Article 16 does not name
-- Article 73. It names Article 17 (a quality management system, which must
-- include reporting PROCEDURES) and Article 20. So for a provider supervised by
-- a national authority, a failure to REPORT under Article 73 has no ceiling in
-- this Regulation: it falls to the Member State rules under Article 99(1).
-- As amended, Article 75c(4)(a) does bring it under the Article 99(4) ceiling
-- for a provider the AI Office supervises.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-domain`
IMPORT `aia-dates`
IMPORT `aia-definitions`
IMPORT `aia-art73`
IMPORT `aia-gpai`

§ `Penalties`

§§ `Article 99(4), (6) and (6a): the ceiling`

-- src:2012 | 4. Non-compliance with any of the following provisions related to operators or notified bodies, other than those laid down in Articles 5, shall be subject to administrative fines of up to EUR 15 000 000 or, if the offender is an undertaking, up to 3 % of its total worldwide annual turnover for the preceding financial year, whichever is higher:
-- src:2028 | 6. In the case of SMEs, including start-ups, each fine referred to in this Article shall be up to the percentages or amount referred to in paragraphs 3, 4 and 5, whichever thereof is lower.
-- src:eu-omnibus-2026-1744:600 | ‘6a. In the case of SMCs, each fine referred to in paragraphs 4 and 5 shall be up to the percentages or amount referred therein, whichever is lower.’
-- As enacted there is no Article 99(6a) and no definition of an SMC, so an
-- SMC takes the general rule, "whichever is higher".
@ref Article 99(4) (src:2012); Article 99(6) (src:2028); Article 99(6a), inserted by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744 Art 1(38)(c) (src:eu-omnibus-2026-1744:600)
GIVEN v IS A `version of the Regulation`, size IS A `size of the provider`, turnover IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Article 99(4) maximum in euros` v size turnover MEANS
    CONSIDER size
    WHEN `not an undertaking` THEN 15_000_000
    WHEN `an SME, including a start-up` THEN min 15_000_000 (3% TIMES turnover)
    WHEN `an SMC, a small mid-cap enterprise` THEN
        CONSIDER v
        WHEN `as enacted` THEN max 15_000_000 (3% TIMES turnover)
        WHEN `as amended by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744` THEN min 15_000_000 (3% TIMES turnover)
    WHEN `another undertaking` THEN max 15_000_000 (3% TIMES turnover)

§§ `Not reporting under Article 73`

-- src:2013 | (a)
-- src:2014 | obligations of providers pursuant to Article 16;
-- src:878 | have a quality management system in place which complies with Article 17;
-- src:917 | procedures related to the reporting of a serious incident in accordance with Article 73;
-- src:2009 | 1. In accordance with the terms and conditions laid down in this Regulation, Member States shall lay down the rules on penalties and other enforcement measures, which may also include warnings and non-monetary measures, applicable to infringements of this Regulation by operators,
-- src:eu-omnibus-2026-1744:591 | ‘1. In accordance with the terms and conditions laid down in this Regulation, Member States shall lay down the rules on penalties and other enforcement measures, which may also include administrative fines, warnings and non-monetary measures, applicable to any infringement of this Regulation by operators,
-- src:eu-omnibus-2026-1744:499 | 4. A decision adopted pursuant to paragraph 1 of this Article may be accompanied by the imposition of penalties in accordance with Article 99(3) to (7), which provisions shall apply mutatis mutandis to the AI Office in the execution of its supervision and enforcement tasks referred to in Article 75(1).
-- src:eu-omnibus-2026-1744:500 | In particular, the following shall be subject to administrative fines as referred to in Article 99(4):
-- src:eu-omnibus-2026-1744:501 | (a)
-- src:eu-omnibus-2026-1744:502 | infringement of any applicable provision of this Regulation, including those not listed in Article 99(4);
-- Article 99(4)(a) reaches the obligations "pursuant to Article 16"; Article
-- 16(c) requires a quality management system complying with Article 17, and
-- Article 17(1)(i) requires reporting PROCEDURES. Not having the procedures is
-- reachable that way; failing to make a report is not named: FORK F8.
-- "Article 99(3) to (7)" in Article 75c(4) is read to include paragraph 6a,
-- which falls between 6 and 7.
@ref Article 99(1) (src:2009), as replaced (src:eu-omnibus-2026-1744:591); Article 99(4)(a) (src:2013-2014); Article 16(c) (src:878); Article 17(1)(i) (src:917); Article 75c(4), inserted by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744 Art 1(32) (src:eu-omnibus-2026-1744:499-502)
GIVEN `the date` IS A DATE, v IS A `version of the Regulation`, s IS AN `AI system facts`, i IS AN `incident facts`, size IS A `size of the provider`, turnover IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `maximum fine`
`the most I can be fined for not reporting under Article 73` `the date` v s i size turnover MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT (`must I report the incident under Article 73` `the date` v s i))
        THEN `no duty applies, so no fine for breaching it`
        IF `the AI Office is exclusively competent for my system` v s
        THEN `up to` (`the Article 99(4) maximum in euros` v size turnover)
        OTHERWISE `no maximum in this Regulation: the Member State rules under Article 99(1)`

§§ `Not informing under Article 20(2)`

-- src:892 | take the necessary corrective actions and provide information as required in Article 20;
-- Article 16(j) names Article 20, so Article 99(4)(a) reaches it.
@ref Article 16(j) (src:892); Article 99(4)(a) (src:2013-2014)
GIVEN `the date` IS A DATE, v IS A `version of the Regulation`, s IS AN `AI system facts`, `it presents a risk within Article 79(1) and I am aware of it` IS A BOOLEAN, size IS A `size of the provider`, turnover IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `maximum fine`
`the most I can be fined for not informing under Article 20(2)` `the date` v s `it presents a risk within Article 79(1) and I am aware of it` size turnover MEANS
    IF `must I inform the market surveillance authorities under Article 20(2)` `the date` v s `it presents a risk within Article 79(1) and I am aware of it`
    THEN `up to` (`the Article 99(4) maximum in euros` v size turnover)
    ELSE `no duty applies, so no fine for breaching it`

§§ `Not reporting under Article 55(1)(c): Article 101`

-- src:2079 | 1. The Commission may impose on providers of general-purpose AI models fines not exceeding 3 % of their annual total worldwide turnover in the preceding financial year or EUR 15 000 000, whichever is higher., when the Commission finds that the provider intentionally or negligently:
-- src:2080 | (a)
-- src:2081 | infringed the relevant provisions of this Regulation;
-- src:2204 | Chapter III Section 4, Chapter V, Chapter VII and Chapter XII and Article 78 shall apply from 2 August 2025, with the exception of Article 101;
-- Article 101 has no SME rule: Article 99(6) speaks of "each fine referred
-- to in this Article", meaning Article 99. So an SME's ceiling here is the
-- same "whichever is higher". The Commission must also find intent or
-- negligence, which is not encoded: this is the ceiling if it does.
-- Before 2 August 2026, Article 101 does not apply (Article 113(b)).
@ref Article 101(1)(a) (src:2079-2081); Article 113(b) (src:2204)
GIVEN `the date` IS A DATE, m IS A `model facts`, i IS AN `incident facts`, turnover IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `maximum fine`
`the most I can be fined for not reporting under Article 55(1)(c)` `the date` m i turnover MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT (`must I report the incident under Article 55(1)(c)` `the date` m i))
        THEN `no duty applies, so no fine for breaching it`
        IF `the date` LESS THAN `Article 101 applies from`
        THEN `no power to fine under this provision applies on that date`
        OTHERWISE `up to` (max 15_000_000 (3% TIMES turnover))
